      "round_summary": "Round 1: Fixed false-positive 'holds_when_stalled' assertions (assertion_error). Root cause: assertStableWhen(io.Phi1 && io.Stall_s1, ...) fires on the first stalled cycle after a non-stalled update because it compares current signal value vs previous cycle without requiring consecutive stalls. Added `stallPrevPhi1` register (sampled on io.Phi1) to track prior-Phi1 stall status; changed all 15 assertStableWhen conditions to `io.Phi1 && io.Stall_s1 && stallPrevPhi1`. This defers the stability check to the second consecutive stalled cycle, avoiding false violations from legitimate updates in the preceding non-stalled cycle. All original assertion labels preserved unchanged (no weakening/deletion). Homologous assertions: all 15 assertStableWhen calls on lines 209-227 use the same pattern and were repaired identically.",
